      "sequence_position": 14,
      "problem": "Let $A=R,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie to the right of the right-opening parabola whose focus is at $(2,0)$ and whose vertex is at $O.$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\nR=\\{{{field-1}}\\in {{field-2}}\\,:\\,{{field-3}}\\}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R$ such that ${y}^{2}<8x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14267010/assets/285ac3df9a33145b24105ed10b2ffbf1dd15523d8bf666b6233e810af23c99ac.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{y}^{2}<8x\\}\n$$",
